# Trust boundaries: the review gate, its authority, the declared panel and
# the workflow that enforces them. Changing any of these can weaken the
# required review check, so they need an owner review.
#
# Enforced only when the branch protection rule on main requires code-owner
# review ("Require review from Code Owners"). The workflow JOB BODY is still
# read from the PR ref (GitHub evaluates pull_request workflows from that
# ref); the verifier, its authority and the panel are checked out from the
# base revision, and this file makes any workflow edit need an owner's
# approval. Admin merges remain the owner's own trust boundary.
